From 0743adab35013dfa619409cb4d66395bcb166f34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:19:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: Don't count a vdev restart as a start

A channel switch restarts the vdev without stopping it, so the started
vdev count went up by one and every later VDEV_STAT request waited the
full 3 s for a second vdev's stats that the firmware never sends.

Suggested-by: Baochen Qiang <baochen.qiang@oss.qualcomm.com>

[ from infiniti-mainline/linux master, commit fd4ee6f55976 ]
[ upstream author: Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev>; picked for the iceland kernel q89 ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index 994a42f6cf..f764462168 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -11491,7 +11491,8 @@ ath12k_mac_vdev_start_restart(struct ath12k_link_vif *arvif,
 						   &arvif->reg_tpc_info);
 	}
 
-	ar->num_started_vdevs++;
+	if (!restart)
+		ar->num_started_vdevs++;
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_MAC,  "vdev %pM started, vdev_id %d\n",
 		   ahvif->vif->addr, arvif->vdev_id);
 
-- 
